      "side": 1,
      "message": "Initially we used the update_device method to change admin state of the device. We expected that device state should change and finally the call back functions should be called as per state transition table in device agent.py. What we observed was, the device_agent propagates the state of the device, but it will not call the call back function as per state transition table.\n\nIn our case, we are trying to update ONU device state from PREPROVISION to ENABLED state, expect device agent to call activate_device function as per state transition table of device_agent.py.\n\"(AdminState.PREPROVISIONED, AdminState.ENABLED): _activate_device,\n\"\nLater, with code browsing, what we understood was the update_device function will only propagate the change in the device and will not do more than that.\n\nTo achieve above said functionality, we introduced new method update_device_state, which follows the similar code of \"update_child_devices_state\".",
